WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:04.560
Another episode of Loki has arrived, bringing&nbsp;
with it some twists, a long-awaited cameo,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.560 --> 00:00:08.960
and even some unexpected romance. What does&nbsp;
it all mean? Where will our favorite God of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:08.960 --> 00:00:13.120
Mischief be heading next? Here's the&nbsp;
ending of Loki episode 4 explained.

00:00:14.240 --> 00:00:16.960
The immediate question coming&nbsp;
out of Episode 3 was how Loki&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.960 --> 00:00:20.800
and Sylvie were going to escape death in&nbsp;
the face of an apocalypse on Lamentis.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.800 --> 00:00:24.960
That kind of life or death situation brings&nbsp;
out some real honesty in both of the two Gods&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.960 --> 00:00:28.800
of Mischief. Faced with the possibility of&nbsp;
being crushed to death, the two grow closer&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.800 --> 00:00:33.040
and Sylvie opens up about why she's trying&nbsp;
to dismantle the Time Variance Authority.

00:00:33.040 --> 00:00:36.800
As it turns out, Ravonna Renslayer is the&nbsp;
Hunter who originally snatched Sylvie from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:36.800 --> 00:00:40.640
Asgard when she was just a young girl, which&nbsp;
we see at the beginning of the episode.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.640 --> 00:00:45.280
The trauma of being ripped away from her home&nbsp;
has given Sylvie the goal of destroying the TVA.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:45.280 --> 00:00:48.720
In any case, Sylvie definitely has&nbsp;
a bone to pick with Ravonna herself,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:48.720 --> 00:00:52.821
blaming the TVA chief for forcing her to grow&nbsp;
up through "the ends of a thousand worlds."

00:00:53.280 --> 00:00:56.560
As Loki and Sylvie await their&nbsp;
doom, the two Variants have a brief,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:56.560 --> 00:01:00.960
tender moment in the face of Armageddon, with&nbsp;
Sylvie affectionately touching Loki's arm.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.960 --> 00:01:04.800
However, when two Variants interact like&nbsp;
that, it creates a new timeline branch,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:04.800 --> 00:01:08.880
which alerts Mobius and the rest of the TVA&nbsp;
to their location so they can retrieve them.

00:01:10.240 --> 00:01:14.560
One of the most surprising moments of the&nbsp;
episode was a delightful cameo from Lady Sif,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:14.560 --> 00:01:19.280
who hasn't appeared in the MCU since "Thor: The&nbsp;
Dark World," unless you count a 2015 episode of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:19.280 --> 00:01:23.040
"Marvel's Agents of SHIELD." Although her&nbsp;
role in the episode is only a minor one,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:23.040 --> 00:01:27.440
it forces Loki to take a closer look&nbsp;
at himself. Mobius traps Loki in a time&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:27.440 --> 00:01:31.760
loop where Sif repeatedly beats him up in&nbsp;
Asgard for cutting off her hair as a joke.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:31.760 --> 00:01:35.520
Sure, the physical beating is torturous,&nbsp;
but it's not the true purpose of the loop.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:35.520 --> 00:01:39.992
Rather, it's what she says to the trickster&nbsp;
that slowly chips away at Loki's resolve:

00:01:39.992 --> 00:01:43.760
"I hope you know you deserve to&nbsp;
be alone and you always will be."

00:01:43.760 --> 00:01:47.200
The God of Mischief has always seen&nbsp;
himself as a loner and an outsider,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:47.200 --> 00:01:51.040
even though he was considered family by&nbsp;
the likes of Thor and Odin. Obviously,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:51.040 --> 00:01:54.400
this version of the character didn't get&nbsp;
the original story arc after the events of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:54.400 --> 00:01:58.240
"The Avengers" that made him realize that&nbsp;
he truly has a family. But this time loop&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:58.240 --> 00:02:02.480
is clearly setting the Asgardian up to realize&nbsp;
that he doesn't want to live like that anymore.

00:02:02.480 --> 00:02:05.600
Additionally, Loki is falling&nbsp;
for Sylvie - something Mobius&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:05.600 --> 00:02:07.840
finds hilarious in his interrogation scene,

00:02:08.480 --> 00:02:14.092
"What an incredible seismic&nbsp;
narcissist! You fell for yourself!"

00:02:14.560 --> 00:02:19.490
Indeed, Loki's in love with himself, a development&nbsp;
that definitely doesn't seem like it will end&nbsp;well. 

00:02:19.490 --> 00:02:23.520
However, Loki's conversation with Mobius&nbsp;
leads to the God of Mischief trying to convince&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:23.520 --> 00:02:27.520
Mobius that everyone at the TVA are actually&nbsp;
variants whose memories have been erased.

00:02:28.720 --> 00:02:31.920
Loki's insistence that Time Keepers&nbsp;
are kidnapping Variants and wiping&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:31.920 --> 00:02:36.000
their memories to work for the TVA pushes&nbsp;
Mobius to look into his claims. In fact,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:36.000 --> 00:02:39.520
it says a lot about the impact Loki&nbsp;
has had on the TVA analyst that he's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:39.520 --> 00:02:43.520
started to take him seriously. Mobius and&nbsp;
Loki have struck up a genuine friendship,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:43.520 --> 00:02:47.537
even if that friendship is based on the two of&nbsp;
them trying to outsmart each other at every turn.

00:02:47.920 --> 00:02:52.240
It's that friendship that makes Mobius sneak a&nbsp;
look at Ravonna's TemPad after she refuses to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:52.240 --> 00:02:56.560
explain what really happened to Hunter C-20,&nbsp;
which allows him to discover that Loki was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:56.560 --> 00:03:00.720
right about the TVA. This means Ravonna&nbsp;
is covering up the Time Keepers' deceit.

00:03:01.280 --> 00:03:04.480
Obviously, Ravonna doesn't want this&nbsp;
information to become public knowledge,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:04.480 --> 00:03:08.400
so when Mobius starts wondering aloud about&nbsp;
what his life was like before being a cosmic&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:08.400 --> 00:03:13.440
bureaucrat, she orders a hunter to prune him.&nbsp;
Hopefully, this isn't the last we see of Mobius.

00:03:14.480 --> 00:03:19.040
Ever since the first episode of "Loki, fans have&nbsp;
suspected that the Time Keepers aren't even real,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:19.040 --> 00:03:23.840
largely because we haven't seen them in action at&nbsp;
all in the series so far. But in a surprise twist,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:23.840 --> 00:03:28.080
Ravonna takes the two Loki Variants to meet&nbsp;
the trio of "Space Lizards" - leading to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:28.080 --> 00:03:32.320
an interesting conversation between the&nbsp;
TVA chief and Sylvie. After everything,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:32.320 --> 00:03:36.863
Sylvie is still desperate for answers about why&nbsp;
her life was thrown into ruin because of the TVA.

00:03:37.360 --> 00:03:41.200
The show still hasn't explained what&nbsp;
Nexus Event made the TVA go after Sylvie,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:41.200 --> 00:03:46.400
and Ravonna isn't about to open up about that just&nbsp;
yet. Instead, she brushes Sylvie's question off,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:46.400 --> 00:03:51.000
saying she doesn't remember why they were sent&nbsp;
after her, which visibly crushes and enrages&nbsp;Sylvie. 

00:03:51.000 --> 00:03:54.160
After an atmospheric battle&nbsp;
in the Time Keeper's smokey chamber,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:54.160 --> 00:03:58.800
the series reveals the three aliens running&nbsp;
the TVA are actually androids... so clearly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:58.800 --> 00:04:03.840
someone else entirely is pulling the TVA's&nbsp;
strings. But who's really behind the TVA?

00:04:03.840 --> 00:04:07.760
Regardless, the Variants have proved that&nbsp;
perhaps a dash of chaos is exactly what&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:07.760 --> 00:04:11.440
the Multiverse needs. They're even on the&nbsp;
cusp of confessing their feelings for one&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:11.440 --> 00:04:15.920
another - a possibility seemingly ruined when&nbsp;
Ravonna prunes Loki right in front of Sylvie.

00:04:16.960 --> 00:04:22.542
But wait - there's more! The series' first&nbsp;
mid-credits scene reveals that Loki might not&nbsp;be dead. &nbsp;

00:04:22.542 --> 00:04:26.880
Once again, the trickster cheats death in&nbsp;
the MCU, and the Asgardian wakes up in what looks&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:26.880 --> 00:04:32.080
like a ruined version of New York asking if he's&nbsp;
in Hel. In response, a dramatic voice replies,

00:04:33.440 --> 00:04:36.880
"Not yet. But you will be,&nbsp;
unless you come with us."

00:04:36.880 --> 00:04:40.960
And that's when the show's biggest twist&nbsp;
yet is revealed, introducing us to four more&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:40.960 --> 00:04:45.840
Loki variants. Is this new world filled with&nbsp;
other dead Lokis? Or is it home to countless&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:45.840 --> 00:04:50.320
pruned Variants from across the multiverse?&nbsp;
Hopefully, Episode 5 will have more answers.

